in 1978 john carpenter's halloween was  released and became an instant hit that  spawned a huge horror franchise it's a  beloved classic but not everything in  the series was well received here are  examples of questionable storylines  with over 10 entries in the halloween  canon it can be challenging to remember  what has happened before any given movie  and that's not entirely the viewer's  fault halloween debuted in 1978 and by  the time halloween h2o 20 years later  was released in 1998 there were six  movies filled with different characters  instead of trying to tie together the  plots of all the films halloween h2o  retconned everything outside of the  original movie and its sequel in this  version of events films four through six  never occurred meaning lori strode never  had a secret daughter who michael myers  murdered instead laurie faked her death  assumed a new identity and had a son  nine years later rob zombie tried his  hand at making a halloween movie but he  started over with a rebooted completely  separate timeline creating his own  version of the characters when the  franchise returned in 2018 for a soft  reboot it erased everything except the  original halloween as if it were a  direct sequel 40 years in the making it  slightly addressed this in the 2018 film  when one character brings up plot points  from 1981's halloween 2 and is bluntly  told those were only rumors though the  branching arcs and characters may  intimidate new viewers at the end of the  day the series is still relatively  straightforward the strode family is  haunted by the trauma of the events of  the original halloween and a relentless  serial killer terrorizes the town of  haddenfield  halloween the curse of michael myers  starts with michael hunting down laurie  strode's 15 year old daughter jamie and  her newborn baby knowing michael is  after her jamie calls into a radio show  to ask michael's former psychiatrist dr  sam loomis for help she then immediately  hides her baby soon after michael finds  and kills jaime but her baby is found by  a grown-up tommy doyle the boy lori was  babysitting in the first film theorizing  that michael is intentionally targeting  members of his own family tommy does his  best to hide the infant from the killer  being the nigh unstoppable killing  machine he is michael eventually catches  up with the baby and in the fabled  producer's cut of the film a character  tries to stop michael from killing the  infant by suggesting it might be his  child since laurie is michael's sister  this presents the idea that he had a son  with his niece the implication of incest  is thankfully omitted in the theatrical  cut which without a doubt makes it the  stronger version given the uncomfortable  nature of this reveal it's probably  better to stick to the wider releases  story and pretend incest never happened  the hectic opening of halloween the  curse of michael myers should tip  viewers off right away that this will  not be an average entry in the franchise  a woman giving birth is surrounded by  doctors wheeling her gurney through an  industrial area then into a stone-carved  cavern lit with torches once the newborn  is delivered it's given to a mysterious  figure before the baby's mother has a  chance to hold him the infant is then  placed on a stone altar and has a symbol  drawn in red on its stomach surrounding  the newborn are three figures clad in  black robes it's unlike anything that's  been seen in a halloween film until this  point in the franchise these robed  figures are the movie's primary villains  and it's eventually revealed that this  cult has found a way to control michael  using an ancient rune of darkness known  as the thorn their claim seems to be  confirmed in the producer's cut when  tommy succeeds in halting michael's  rampage by using ancient runes of light  however thanks to difficulties with the  production the cult storyline never  fully took shape and it's no wonder that  future sequels let it go all together  though donald pleasence died  unexpectedly in 1995 he remains a  fixture of the halloween franchise  thanks to his character dr sam loomis  and his importance in the michael myers  story having been assigned to michael's  case dr loomis had 15 years to treat the  boy by the time of the first film he  decided michael was no longer a man but  evil in a human shape who had no chance  of redemption i realized that what was  living behind that boy's eyes was purely  and simply  evil from the moment michael escapes dr  loomis is hell-bent on taking michael  down by any means necessary this  includes blowing himself up traumatizing  children giving a bunch of locals  inferred permission to patrol the town  with rifles and holding police officers  at gunpoint throughout the series the  authority figures who interact with  loomis repeatedly dismiss the doctor and  underplay michael's threat to their  communities this isn't restricted to  police chiefs sheriffs or government  officials even the psychiatrist's  colleagues believe he should be  receiving mental health counseling  instead of dispensing it while he is  undoubtedly obsessive dr loomis is  almost always right whenever he suspects  michael is at large the only time dr  loomis is repeatedly wrong is in his  guesses of how to kill michael myers no  matter how many times he tried loomis  could never quite get rid of his least  favorite patient  there are numerous shots throughout the  halloween franchise of michael locking  eyes with his victims in a menacing  fashion these are always tense moments  as they often signal the victim  beginning to understand the danger  they're truly in these shots also have a  sort of calm before the storm vibe to  them focusing on stillness and inaction  to better punctuate the frantic fleeing  and stabbing that is usually about to  commence however one odd choice  throughout the franchise is the tendency  to follow a specific sequence of shots  in these interactions first the camera  shows michael staring at his victim what  follows is a reverse shot of the victim  looking at michael then the camera cuts  back to where the character is staring  only to show an empty michaelis space  sometimes this gives michael the  appearance of teleporting as the  character's gaze doesn't tend to follow  him to where he might have moved while  this is obviously an attempt by the  filmmakers to make michael myers more  threatening it actually raises more  questions than it answers in a matter of  seconds michael seemingly warps across  the room or safely off screen breaking  some of the tension that was previously  in the scene though it may admittedly be  awkward to watch michael walk from point  a to point b in every instance some  creative editing may help to make these  moments more believable by the time  halloween the curse of michael myers  happens 17 years have passed since  michael escaped from the institution in  which he was previously imprisoned for  15 years for murdering his older sister  upon obtaining his freedom he returned  to his hometown of haddenfield to attack  high school babysitter lori strode who  was later revealed to be his younger  sister this means michael's murders have  haunted the town for years however the  curse of michael myers is the first time  the holiday seems to have been curtailed  by the local government ahead of time in  fact when the film takes place  haddonfield residents are just beginning  to fight back against the restrictions  it seems odd that haddenfield would go  so far as to restrict the public  celebration of a holiday entirely and  especially odd that they only thought to  do it 30 some years after the first  meyer's murder aside from the two  halloweens where michael murdered one  sister then attempted to murder his  other one there have been several  incidents that probably should have been  on local officials radars in halloween 4  the return of michael myers one of the  local problems is that so many kids have  dressed up as their town's favorite  serial killer that it's hard to find the  real one a similar problem presents  itself in the following film the revenge  of michael myers where a local kid  dresses like michael as a joke allowing  people to mistake the real killer for a  teenager messing with his friends  instead of banning the whole holiday it  seems like banning the costume may have  been a better choice  rob zombie's halloween films are  contentious among fans of the franchise  while some admire the depth of backstory  from michael myers others find that the  characterization diminishes his impact  and is unnecessary however what most  fans agree on is that rob zombie's  halloween 2 is one of the most bizarre  entries in the series feeling much more  like a hyper stylized rob zombie acid  horror trip than a halloween film to  some extent zombies halloween 2 follows  similar story beats to the original  halloween 2. both films confirmed that  lori strode and michael myers are  siblings but unlike the original zombies  halloween 2 focuses more on the  psychological aspect of the characters  and delves into surrealist territory the  film features several hallucinations  that link the siblings minds including  scenes in which lori begins to envision  herself carrying out michael's past  murders eventually laurie is sent to an  institution similar to the one that held  her brother for 15 years here we see the  most outlandish imagery in the entirety  of the halloween franchise a  hallucination of a white horse that  feels more akin to a fantasy film than  something that should be in halloween  too overall zombies halloween 2 is one  of the oddest films in the franchise and  the abstract nature of the movie is  often forgotten or ignored when  discussing some of the latter more  disliked films in the series  one of the most effective ways to make a  horror film scary is through clever  sound design most people familiar with  jump scares know that music and sound  effects are frequently used to get a  reaction out of audience members beyond  jump scares and the use of a film's  score sound effects that aren't made to  scare in and of themselves can be hugely  effective in ratcheting up the tension  of any given scene for instance the  metallic shing of a knife as it's drawn  helps reinforce its sharpness in the  mind of audience members and the loud  thwack that rings out when the same  blade is plunged into its target can  make the impact seem much more  terrifying than the visual alone with so  much potential to enhance the mood of a  scene the misuse of sound effects is  often glaring and can take the viewer  right out of the movie while the  halloween films generally use sound  effects well there are a few  unforgettable instances where they feel  distinctly out of place the best example  of this is found in halloween 5 the  revenge of michael myers during a  comedic scene between two police  officers a series of clown sound effects  including honking are played during  their banter without any explanation  fortunately we're lousy cops  sorry halloween resurrection features a  group of teens wandering around the  abandoned myers house on a halloween  night as part of an internet live stream  this reality show functions by having  all the cameras accessible for audiences  to watch at any time and the contestant  that most viewers choose to watch is the  winner however little do the  participants or the show's producers  know that michael myers has made his way  back to his childhood home and he's  ready to kill anyone he gets his hands  on when it becomes clear to audiences  that contestants are actually being  murdered and aren't playing pranks on  the others for views the mood inside and  outside the house becomes less  lighthearted luckily one contestant has  a friend watching who texts her  michael's location while checking other  cameras this ends up saving her life a  couple of times and even earns the guy a  shout out once reporters show up to get  a statement from the survivor who's  still wrapped in a shock blanket while  this works well for the characters in  the film it seems a bit suspect that a  live stream with upwards of a dozen  cameras all broadcasting live would have  no lag while operating within a small  illinois town's 2002 internet  infrastructure aside from having  instantaneous uploading there also  appears to be no issue with buffering or  loading on the viewing end as up to the  second info on michael is sent via text  even if the show was done today there  would likely be at least a several  second long delay for viewers at home  and certainly a few more seconds to wait  for a text message to send check out one  of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite horror movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

